From: stew675 <stew675@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 23:40:15 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] wip/prefill-decode-arms pass 1: T1 (the slot handover) done
 and text-exact, the two arms emulated outside the server, three new landmines

T1: enabling-0002-recurrent-handover.patch -- one sequence's recurrent state moves between the two arms
device-to-device in 0.5-0.7 ms (36 ms serialised, 52.7 MiB through host memory).  Text oracle: exact on a
no-host-tier 4B in every mode/repetition, and on the 35B host tier for a single handed-over request (3/3 warm
reps).

The instrument arms/two_arms.cpp is the server's shape without the server (two contexts, one KV, two threads, a
request queue, the handover at the request boundary) and reproduces the campaign's physics: 38 decoder tokens
through a 2.08 s prefill at ITL p50 53.7 / p95 71.6 ms for +14.1 % prefill (6.75 ms charged per decoder token,
against the retired campaign's 7.7 ms at the same arena).

Landmines: (1) the shared KV's cell allocator is not concurrency-safe (find_slot searches from v_heads,
apply_ubatch advances it afterwards -- two allocating arms can be handed the same cells); (2) the second arm's
VRAM is a graph reserve per arm AND per active-slot width (741 MiB for 2 rows), so arena 5000 + -ub 2048 does not
fit on a 32 GiB card; (3) a 2-slot two-arm decode is not text-stable across warm reps -- isolated against the
handover, DEVREMAP, PREFILL_IN_PLACE, the overlap and the host tier, so T3's gate must pin the shape and add the
KLD point.

No delivery patch changed, no block created or amended, no tag.  ~/llama.cpp carries the change on the WIP
branch wip/prefill-overlap only.
